Urgh."#It kinda tickles my stomach...":The Doctrine was down here before too, were they not?"|In truth, I don't particularly fear or loathe the Doctrine as many others do, but I do wonder what they could be planning..."MMaybe finding the archives could give us insight into their motivations?"fAlthough, I'd be lying if I said I wanted to find the archives for some heroic purpose like that.";I'm just so very curious as to what they could hold..."'The wild Chikorita fled southeast!"#The wild Chikorita fled above!"2Our designs are blessed by the lord Giratina."Heresy!"-You blasphemers will meet your end soon."BLisa-Marie: These structures must be hundreds of years old..."3I wonder who built them, and for what purpose?"5Let's press further, to the heart of the forest!"Let's get this over with."Oh well."&It's not like I can stop you now."(Pride: D'you two know what this is?"2Percy: Looks like a statue of a... Tangrowth."]I'm assuming there's something special about it, unless you came here just to admire it."ePride: These statues're known as Temple Guardians. There're eighteen scattered throughout Zakos."FWhat I'm here for ain't the statue though, but what it's holdin'." Percy: What <i>is</i> that?"It's... humming.":Pride: You can feel the energy it's releasin', right?">That's how a forest this big is able to grow underground." Pretty damn cool, ain't it?"EPercy: What could you possibly be planning on doing with that..."8Pride: Looks like you'll just have to wait and see."<Percy: Like we're just going to let you. Get ready \PN."/Pride: Lemme guess what's about to happen."`Y'all are gonna try and stop me even though neither of you know what we're really plannin'."?And then I'll beat the living hell out of y'all in battle."RPercy: I don't like fighting at all, and I certainly don't want to fight you."7But it's looking like we don't have a choice here."Pride: Fair point, kid."II wasn't plannin' on letting you kids go anyways, fight or no fight."9Can't wait to wipe y'all off the bottom of my boots."No no NO!""Pride: How'd, \|how'd I lose?"7Percy: Not as confident as you were before, Pride?"BPride: Y'all got some insane luck or today's just not my day."SEven with you two cheatin' by teamin' up I should've been able to floor y'all."IPride: Well, I was told not to use brute force but who gives a damn."2Pride: We're done here Edgar. Let's head out."EPercy: If he could've done that at the beginning, why didn't he?"LYou don't think the temple has like, some sort of defense system right?"pPercy: Shit, I shouldn't have said anything. \PN, hold off the Tangrowth while I deal with the little ones!"Percy: What was that?"LHe took that thing from the Tangrowth and it just started attacking us."iWe should probably tell Minerva what happened, and then, try to figure out what the hell's going on."I'll head down, \PN."Lux: Impressive."And hello again, \PN."eBefore you ask, yes I was watching this whole ordeal, and no, I had no desire to assist you two."ÖThat said, if you two truly knew what they were planning, you would've tried harder to stop Pride from getting the True Meadow Plate."&...Although, that's a bit unfair."DAfter all, there's <i>no way</i> you could've known, was there?"3The Doctrine isn't evil, \PN. No one truly is."PTheir current goal is the consequence of a single person's selfish actions."uAnd if there is any fairness in this world, it will correct itself and none of us will have to worry any longer."6Perhaps once you learn the truth to everything..."QAsk Minerva about the Drowned City. You'll get some of the answers you seek."Farewell \PN."@We're just trying to save everyone from the High Architect!"You should be on our side!"XThe High Architect doesn't forgive, but His Shadow does. It's not too late for you."=How'd you make it this far? The others must be slacking.""Maybe you're just too strong."9The boss is on this floor. He'll teach you a lesson."HThe strongest, most fervent of us were placed closer to the temple."Forgive me.""The Mirror blesses all of us.Iu;␀Â[[>"Beautiful.";That's the only word to describe a place such as this."rWith the flora having grown throughout the temple, it almost looks straight out of a fairy tale, does it not?"gMaybe the temple was built this way, to look as if nature had erupted through the floor and walls."#Isn't that an amusing thought?"|I was thinking that this temple would give us clues as to where the archives might be located, as both are underground."1But it looks as though this is not the case.")The search doesn't end here however!"WMeet me at the Apolvita Grove, I have what you would call a good hunch about this!"LMinerva: I'm going to look around here a bit. You should go help Percy."6Minerva: Percy was just telling me what happened."tI'm not sure what the Tangrowth could've been holding, nor why it would trigger the statue to suddenly animate."fTo be entirely fair though, I wasn't aware that this temple existed at all until a few hours ago."IIt appears I'll have to investigate this temple and the forest more."9Percy: What could the Doctrine possibly be planning?"]Minerva: I'll look into it. I do have quite a bit of scholarly resources at my disposal."..." Percy: Lux showed up again?"rWhat's her deal? There's no way you and her are "old friends", you and Kara were stuck on that island, right?"(Kara complained to no end about it."-Minerva: That aside... the Drowned City."9I did promise a battle for helping me out, didn't I?"/Percy: I'll pass. Battling isn't my thing."`Minerva: Well, when you're ready, \PN, meet me in the library. I hold all my battles there."?Once you have my key, we'll talk about what this Lux said."1Some things are starting to fall into place."MPercy: Good luck \PN. I'll meet up with you once you finish your battle."*Do you want to head to town together?"APercy: I told Minerva what happened. You should talk to her."PMinerva: \PN, Percy? Someone's been waiting here. Apparently they know you?"Percy: Huh?"Percy: Oh 