Psst."4Were you the one who answered the Help Request?"Okay, okay."2They might be listening, so I can't say much-"'But they watch me everywhere I go."The shadows."-Please drive them away, I'm begging you."LIf I'm seeing them everywhere, you shouldn't have trouble finding them."Please..."Are they gone?"For real?"..."Oh, thank god.""You definitely deserve these."\PN received 12 AP!")I can finally stop watching my back-"Thanks a ton.Iu;␀z[["2Hestia: Agrus should be in the tent up north."!Hestia: Good luck out there."/Hestia: You guys did it, I'm proud of you."3Hestia: Hope there's no more hiccups out here.";It's rough out there, maybe my moves can help you out?" That'll be two blue shards."(This one's gonna be two red shards."Alright I guess."Yes"No"Uproar"Worry Seed"	None[@@@	@
@@@@@@@@@;["2Hestia: Agrus should be in the tent up north."!Hestia: Good luck out there."/Hestia: You guys did it, I'm proud of you."3Hestia: Hope there's no more hiccups out here.";It's rough out there, maybe my moves can help you out?" That'll be two blue shards."(This one's gonna be two red shards."Alright I guess."Yes"No"Uproar"Worry Seed"	NoneIu;␀«[["@There's a cemetery nearby where a pack of dog Pokemon live.".I wonder who the leader of the pack is..."5Maybe getting rid of them all would coax it out?"7I found this doll when I was exploring the forest."1It looks like a Golurk, do you wanna see it?"0It's a crude idol of a Golurk made of clay." It's pretty cool, isn't it?"Why'd you do that?!"(I can't even look at you right now."Yes"No"Give it back."Destroy it.[@@@	@
@@@@@@@@@;["@There's a cemetery nearby where a pack of dog Pokemon live.".I wonder who the leader of the pack is..."5Maybe getting rid of them all would coax it out?"7I found this doll when I was exploring the forest."1It looks like a Golurk, do you wanna see it?"0It's a crude idol of a Golurk made of clay." It's pretty cool, isn't it?"Why'd you do that?!"(I can't even look at you right now."Yes"No"Give it back."Destroy it.Iu;␀[[␀[␀;[␀Iu;␀	[[""Minerva: Welcome."VThis is a storage space where we keep items not ready to be shelved or displayed."4Or items we want to keep out of the public eye."+Now let's get to it, the Drowned City."êLong ago, before the Church of Arceus or the Doctrine of Giratina came into existence, there was a single religion that those in Zakos followed."hThose that followed this religion revered all legendary Pokemon, worshipping them indiscriminately."?Percy: ...What does this have to do with the Drowned City?" Minerva: I'm getting there."ïMinerva: Rumor goes that ancient followers of this religion constructed a massive city made up of temples, with a chamber for each legendary Pokemon."êThe ancient religion eventually split into the Church and the Doctrine, but it's rumoured that the sinking of the temple-city is what caused it."ÉOf course, this is all theoretical. There's no evidence that such a city exists, and no leads as to where it might even be located."Percy: But...?"dMinerva: At least, that's what I thought until I inherited the Hierophant's Key from my father."WThese are the only texts that survived the fire that burned the library years ago."íThere is one in particular that details the creation of a massive temple-city, created as a conduit to "speak to the Gods", whatever that entails."1Percy: That has to be the Drowned City then!"¶Minerva: It's likely so. Unfortunately, we're still a fair bit off from understanding what exactly the Doctrine is planning, and the nature of the Underground Forest.";Percy: Lux didn't tell you anything else, did she \PN?"..."gMinerva: The True Meadow Plate? Well, I can't say I know what that is, but it does give us a lead."`I'll try and learn what I can, and if you two find out any more, don't hesitate to tell me."}Percy: Lux, whoever she is, definitely knows a lot more than she's letting on, and she seems to have a weird interest in \PN."Minerva: Well, that's all."0I'll be off then, be sure to keep in touch."Percy: Will do."?Minerva: And good luck with challenging the Pantheon, \PN."[Percy: Oh, congrats for beating Minerva, though in all honesty, I'm not too surprised.""It's still really impressive."SWell, I'll head to Logium Town C and wait for you and Kara then, like planned.["@@@	@
@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@ @!@"@#;[""Minerva: Welcome."VThis is a storage space where we keep items not ready to be shelved or displayed."4Or items we want to keep out of the public eye."+Now let's get to it, the Drowned City."êLong ago, before the Church of Arceus or the Doctrine of Giratina came into existence, there was a single religion that those in Zakos followed."hThose that followed this religion revered all legendary Pokemon, worshipping them indiscriminately."?Percy: ...What does this have to do with the Drowned City?" Minerva: I'm getting there."ïMinerva: Rumor goes that ancient followers of this religion constructed a massive city made up of temples, with a chamber for each legendary Pokemon."êThe ancient religion eventually split into the Church and the Doctrine, but it's rumoured that the sinking of the temple-city is what caused it."ÉOf course, this is all theoretical. There's no evidence that such a city exists, and no leads as to where it might even be located."Percy: But...?"dMinerva: At least, that's what I thought until I inherited the Hierophant's Key from my father."WThese are the only texts that survived the fire that burned the library years ago."íThere is one in particular that details the creation of a massive temple-city, created as a conduit to "speak to the Gods", whatever that entails."1Percy: That has to be the Drowned City then!"¶Minerva: It's likely so. Unfortunately, we're still a fair bit off from understanding what exactly the Doctrine is planning, and the nature of the Underground Forest.";Percy: Lux didn't tell you anything else, did she \PN?"..."gMinerva: The True Meadow Plate? Well, I can't say I know what that is, but it does give us a lead."`I'll try and learn what I can, and if you two find out any more, don't hesitate to tell me."}Percy: Lux, whoever she is, definitely knows a lot more than she's letting on, and she seems to have a weird interest in \PN."Minerva: Well, that's all."0I'll be off then, be sure to keep in touch."Percy: Will do."?Minerva: And good luck with challenging the Pantheon, \PN."[Percy: Oh, congrats for beating Minerva, though in all honesty, I'm not too surprised.""It's still really impressive."SWell, I'll head to Logium Town C and wait for you and Kara then, like planned.Iu;␀R[[	"␀" Your party has been healed!"HEALING PARTY..."Well done![	@@@	@
