" Your party has been healed!"HEALING PARTY..."/I'm in charge of the supplies around here."/A good ranger always keeps berries around!"Good luck out there!Iu;␀$[[è"Zossie: \PN! Come here!"3Data: Glad to see you two made it here safely."A\PN, Zossie, this is Agrus, the captain of the rangers here."Agrus: Uh, howdy."YData here was tellin' me that y'all were lookin' for some sorta... space time thing?"Data: A spacetime anomaly."tAgrus: Well, I'm not too sure I can help ya out there, but there're plenty of odd things happenin' 'round here."LWe came here 'cause Olga asked me to search for one of her girls, Rose."GThought it'd be a one and done job, find this chick, and head out."SBut we found out real soon that there was no way to go deeper into the forest."?The heavier the hail got, the more my men lost themselves."PSo, we decided to set up camp here to come up with a plan, and here we are."&Data: Yes, the hail is quite odd."VCalypsan Island is largely tropical, much more so than the mainland to the north."CThere can be no natural cause for this weather like this here."Agrus: The hail ain't all."KThe islands down here are known for havin' pools of water underground."hWe found one of these on the beach when we were settin' up camp, but it was completely frozen over."%Not a drop of water to be found."WData: Strange. The clime here is simply too warm for the ground to freeze as well."!Zossie: Hey! I have an idea!"BWhat if the anomaly we're looking for is causing all of this?"4Data: Excellent deduction, my thoughts exactly."9It appears we have a reason to work together, Agrus."Agrus: Works fer me."EHavin' more hands 'round here means we can get this done faster."Zossie: So... what now?"EAgrus: There's not really much to do 'ccept head back out there."tOh, but y'all will need the HM Cut to head deeper though. The Demesne is pretty thick, lotsa stuff to cut down."OData: This shouldn't be an issue for Zossie and I, but what about you \PN?"..."MAgrus: Well, I can give ya the HM, but do ya got a license of some sort?"nA field license lets ya use all the HMs, or maybe ya gotta job license that lets ya use Cut specifically." Agrus: Collectin' the keys?"Well, yer in luck then."[The name's Agrus Kos, holder of the Hermit's Key, which happens to be the one ya need."Zossie: Keys?"5Data: It's a kingmaking tradition here in Zakos."8Think of them as odd Gym Leaders or Trial Captains."Zossie: Oh!"+Does that mean you'll battle him, \PN?"!Data, Data, can we go watch?"=Data: I'm afraid not. We have some preparations to make."Zossie: Awh..."aAgrus: Hold on, I ain't battlin' you for free though, yer gonna do a lil' task for me first."MMy rangers have brought everyone y'all passed on the way here into camp."6But there's bound to be some stragglers, ya feel?"\Yer gonna head out there with me so we can bring 'em back, and then we can duke it out." Alrighty, let's get movin'!"Good luck \PN!"}Data: Be careful out there. When Zossie and Percy tried to explain what happened, we inexplicably lost contact with him."gAs the hail grows heavier, we can only surmise that more of these odd occurrences will take place."UI trust you will make quick work of this task \PN. We do not have time to waste."^Agrus: Aight, if ya think ya can battle me and win, then this should be no issue fer you."Let's do this thing."PViolet: Before we begin, it only seems proper that I get my saviors' names.",Agrus: I'm Agrus, and this here is \PN."DViolet: Lovely to meet you two, and thanks again for saving me."=Agrus: It ain't no big deal, but let's cut to the chase."Who are you?"aViolet: I presume this question is deeper than just my name, which I have already given you."AI am Violet Koneli, a groundskeeper of sorts on this island."LMy husband, Myron Koneli, is the owner of the very land you stand upon."0Agrus: Koneli... as in, the Koneli Demesne?"[Violet: Indeed, it shares our surname, as we were once a member of the Great Families."`Alas, it was at Myron's hands that our legacy was undone and we were consigned to oblivion."êAnd he intends on doing it again, only this time, it will cost the lives of you two, your comrades, and every other living thing on this island."CAgrus: That's... so this snowstorm is the doin' of this Myron?"NViolet: Yes, it primarily serves as a method of keeping you trapped here."9Agrus: But why? Ya were his wife, right? Do ya know?"/Violet: I know why, but I do not know how."ìMyron lives in the Koneli Manor, deeper in the Demesne. I can lead you two there, as recompense for saving me. You'll better understand on the way.">You both have a reason to stop his machinations, as do I."OAgrus: Right... then let's hurry up this battle so ya can get my key, \PN."sViolet: I shall remain here. Make haste you two, Myron will not wait for anyone and he <i>must</i> be stopped."kAgrus: Meet me in the frozen cave on the shore, but a lil' warnin': I ain't goin' easy no matter what."UViolet: As for you, you've already begun to suspect my true nature, haven't you?"2After all, we're not so different, you and I."Well then, carry on \PN."Hurry, little \PN."5Agrus: Well, I guess introductions are in order."YI'm Agrus Kos, Hyacinth Amphitrite is the guy next to me, and that's \PN over there."???: I am Shago Dasos."And this is Koda Vouno."(Hyacinth: Your names seem familiar."Agrus: Koda Vouno..."?Agrus: Ya used to be the Ranger Knight-Captain, didn't ya?"5But apparently ya disappeared forty years ago..."(Hyacinth: Ah right, I remember now."pI read about you two in a history book, that you two were keyholders who mysteriously disappeared together."Shago: A history book."!I still cannot believe it..."hKoda: The two that freed us did mention that we had been in the stasis tanks for about forty years."7Still, it's difficult to... wrap our heads around."RAgrus: A stasis tank... so ya two were in Myron's hostage room for that long?"(Hyacinth: What happened to you two?"&Koda: It's a bit of a long story."{Shago: King Joseph had instructed us to infiltrate the Koneli Demesne, in order to update him on the Doctrine's activities."jKoda: This was when the Demesne was heavily populated, nothing like the ruins we just walked through."?Shago: But we got caught by the Sin of Wrath, Elmin Agnes."cHe dragged us down to the Spooky Temple and attempted to execute us using the Temple Guardian."XKoda: His daughter Krista got in the way however, and it hurt her badly. Poor girl."kShago: We rushed over to help her, we were not about to stand by and watch someone die in front of us.";That was when the Sin of Pride, Myron Koneli appeared."SKoda: He told us that there was one way we could help, by being test subjects."uBefore we could react, he had grabbed the True Spooky Plate from the Guardian Mismagius and knocked us out cold."ZShago: The last thing I remember was being lowered into the stasis tank, half asleep."5Hyacinth: And he kept you there for forty years?".The Doctrine's cruelty knows no bounds..."(Agrus: ...No, it's not that simple."|This lines up with what Myron's wife told us, that Myron had taken the True Spooky Plate one day, and it drove him mad."IWhen he tried to dispose of it, it devoured everyone on the Demesne."4Koda: ...So that's why no one tried to free us."0There was no one on the Demesne left alive."-Shago: And we were consigned to history."DHyacinth: So why did you want to meet with us specifically now?"}Koda: The two people in the spacesuits that freed us mentioned there were two keyholders and a challenger in your group."IShago: We wanted to ask what had happened over the past forty years."WKoda: We were keyholders, but I'm assuming our positions were stripped since then?"VHyacinth: If I recall correctly, Koda's key was given to the Vice-Captain, Vaxos.".Agrus: He's the Captain now, an' my boss."mKoda: Ah, I remember Vaxos. He has a good head on his shoulders, I'm glad he has taken up my old mantle."Shago: And my key?".Hyacinth: Given to your daughter, Spiria."-Shago: Very well. An acceptable outcome."?Agrus: So, what now? Are ya gonna take yer positions back?"DKoda: I don't intend to. It's a burden I'm glad to be freed of."kShago: I am happy that my daughter has inherited my position. I do not intend on taking that from her."PHyacinth: But I presume you two are planning on heading back to your homes?"@Koda: Of course. I want to see how my loved ones are doing."Shago: Me as well."GHyacinth: I have a proposition for you before you two leave, then."aMiss Olga requested that I challenge \PN for a keyholder battle whenever I come across them."mGiven that you two are our elders, by technicality, I would appreciate your presence whilst this occurs."Koda: I don't see why not."1Shago: Why not. I do enjoy watching battles."zHyacinth: Perfect. Rose says that there are some ruins right outside the encampment that will make for a good battle."Meet me there, \PN."Agrus: Good luck \PN."_I dunno what to think about all this yet, but jus' focus on the battle, and give him hell."$Koda: Perform well for us, \PN."%Shago: You look just like him..."Shago: Could it be...?[è@@@	@
