eli Demesne?"[Violet: Indeed, it shares our surname, as we were once a member of the Great Families."`Alas, it was at Myron's hands that our legacy was undone and we were consigned to oblivion."êAnd he intends on doing it again, only this time, it will cost the lives of you two, your comrades, and every other living thing on this island."CAgrus: That's... so this snowstorm is the doin' of this Myron?"NViolet: Yes, it primarily serves as a method of keeping you trapped here."9Agrus: But why? Ya were his wife, right? Do ya know?"/Violet: I know why, but I do not know how."ìMyron lives in the Koneli Manor, deeper in the Demesne. I can lead you two there, as recompense for saving me. You'll better understand on the way.">You both have a reason to stop his machinations, as do I."OAgrus: Right... then let's hurry up this battle so ya can get my key, \PN."sViolet: I shall remain here. Make haste you two, Myron will not wait for anyone and he <i>must</i> be stopped."kAgrus: Meet me in the frozen cave on the shore, but a lil' warnin': I ain't goin' easy no matter what."UViolet: As for you, you've already begun to suspect my true nature, haven't you?"2After all, we're not so different, you and I."Well then, carry on \PN."Hurry, little \PN."5Agrus: Well, I guess introductions are in order."YI'm Agrus Kos, Hyacinth Amphitrite is the guy next to me, and that's \PN over there."???: I am Shago Dasos."And this is Koda Vouno."(Hyacinth: Your names seem familiar."Agrus: Koda Vouno..."?Agrus: Ya used to be the Ranger Knight-Captain, didn't ya?"5But apparently ya disappeared forty years ago..."(Hyacinth: Ah right, I remember now."pI read about you two in a history book, that you two were keyholders who mysteriously disappeared together."Shago: A history book."!I still cannot believe it..."hKoda: The two that freed us did mention that we had been in the stasis tanks for about forty years."7Still, it's difficult to... wrap our heads around."RAgrus: A stasis tank... so ya two were in Myron's hostage room for that long?"(Hyacinth: What happened to you two?"&Koda: It's a bit of a long story."{Shago: King Joseph had instructed us to infiltrate the Koneli Demesne, in order to update him on the Doctrine's activities."jKoda: This was when the Demesne was heavily populated, nothing like the ruins we just walked through."?Shago: But we got caught by the Sin of Wrath, Elmin Agnes."cHe dragged us down to the Spooky Temple and attempted to execute us using the Temple Guardian."XKoda: His daughter Krista got in the way however, and it hurt her badly. Poor girl."kShago: We rushed over to help her, we were not about to stand by and watch someone die in front of us.";That was when the Sin of Pride, Myron Koneli appeared."SKoda: He told us that there was one way we could help, by being test subjects."uBefore we could react, he had grabbed the True Spooky Plate from the Guardian Mismagius and knocked us out cold."ZShago: The last thing I remember was being lowered into the stasis tank, half asleep."5Hyacinth: And he kept you there for forty years?".The Doctrine's cruelty knows no bounds..."(Agrus: ...No, it's not that simple."|This lines up with what Myron's wife told us, that Myron had taken the True Spooky Plate one day, and it drove him mad."IWhen he tried to dispose of it, it devoured everyone on the Demesne."4Koda: ...So that's why no one tried to free us."0There was no one on the Demesne left alive."-Shago: And we were consigned to history."DHyacinth: So why did you want to meet with us specifically now?"}Koda: The two people in the spacesuits that freed us mentioned there were two keyholders and a challenger in your group."IShago: We wanted to ask what had happened over the past forty years."WKoda: We were keyholders, but I'm assuming our positions were stripped since then?"VHyacinth: If I recall correctly, Koda's key was given to the Vice-Captain, Vaxos.".Agrus: He's the Captain now, an' my boss."mKoda: Ah, I remember Vaxos. He has a good head on his shoulders, I'm glad he has taken up my old mantle."Shago: And my key?".Hyacinth: Given to your daughter, Spiria."-Shago: Very well. An acceptable outcome."?Agrus: So, what now? Are ya gonna take yer positions back?"DKoda: I don't intend to. It's a burden I'm glad to be freed of."kShago: I am happy that my daughter has inherited my position. I do not intend on taking that from her."PHyacinth: But I presume you two are planning on heading back to your homes?"@Koda: Of course. I want to see how my loved ones are doing."Shago: Me as well."GHyacinth: I have a proposition for you before you two leave, then."aMiss Olga requested that I challenge \PN for a keyholder battle whenever I come across them."mGiven that you two are our elders, by technicality, I would appreciate your presence whilst this occurs."Koda: I don't see why not."1Shago: Why not. I do enjoy watching battles."zHyacinth: Perfect. Rose says that there are some ruins right outside the encampment that will make for a good battle."Meet me there, \PN."Agrus: Good luck \PN."_I dunno what to think about all this yet, but jus' focus on the battle, and give him hell."$Koda: Perform well for us, \PN."%Shago: You look just like him..."Shago: Could it be...?Iu;␀d [[í"Agrus: Violet."0Violet: I was so sure they were here too..."$Agrus: The person followin' us?"FViolet: Yes, I thought I felt something follow me in here, but..."Agrus: Never mind that.";I have a question for ya, and I'm just gonna be blunt."Violet: ...Go on."Agrus: Is Myron dead?"AHave ya just been leading us on this‚Ä¶ \|wild Swanna chase?"+Violet: ...Who did you hear that from?"RAgrus: \PN ran into someone earlier, it was probably the person followin' us."Violet: So they knew‚Ä¶"4I was hoping to tell you myself later, but yes."Myron is dead."KBut I did not lie to you. He is still the one behind your predicament."HAgrus: Are ya really tryin' to tell us a dead guy's doing all this?"sViolet: Is it so hard to believe? After all, you've been talking to someone who was dead once this whole time."Agrus: Yer-")???: So that's what's been going on-"4???: I knew following you was a good idea, \PN~":Violet: So you were the one who spilled to these two."How did you know?"E???: Myron used to be one of our own. Of course I'd know, silly."$Agrus: Yer with the Doctrine‚Ä¶"A???: Mhm! I don't have a name, but most people call me Envy~"MViolet: What business does a Doctrine Elder have here? Is it with Myron?"OEnvy: Well, Myron still kicking around wasn't something I even considered."JI am curious though, you and him are both supposed to be dead, right?"So‚Ä¶ how are you, \|not?"Violet: ...I wish I knew."1A few days ago, I just woke up in the manor."\Myron and my children were back as well, along with everyone else who had died with us.";Agrus: Y'all died at the same time? How'd that happen?"%Violet: It wasn't Myron's fault."6No, it was that <i>thing</i> he brought with him."3Envy: Well, this confirms a suspicion of ours."Violet: ...What?"]Envy: The reason I'm here is because of a <i>little</i> mistake one of my brothers made."üHe brute forced the plate out of the Meadow Temple close to here, and we were afraid the resulting shockwave might have awakened the other temples in the area."And well‚Ä¶")Agrus: So this is all y'all's fault?"-Envy: I <i>did</i> say it was a mistake."VThis is good news though! So I can just take the plate and then skedaddle, right?"çViolet: Well, you could, but if the Temple Guardian isn't defeated when the plate is removed, it'll just be a repeat of what happened before."(Everyone on the island will perish."VEnvy: Except for me, because I'll have grabbed the plate and left by then, right?"Agrus: What are ya sayin'-"MEnvy: I do have to thank you guys, this was all very useful information.")Nevertheless, looks like I gotta go~"What's going on?"Violet: What?""I thought I was battling her-"+Were we just battling each other, \PN?";Agrus: I thought I saw ya two battlin' her together..."Violet: ...She duped us."Agrus: Another trick."9Never mind that, we can always apprehend Envy later."=What exactly is Myron's plan? It's high time ya tell us."%Violet: I suppose I owe you two."hSo, those who are devoured by the Spooky Plate become a part of it, they cannot leave its vicinity."|Myron hopes that feeding you all to the plate will allow its influence to spread wide enough that he can escape the Demesne."Agrus: And then?"≠Violet: Well, once he is elsewhere, he can repeat this process over and over until the plate's influence spreads across the world, and he is able to travel where he pleases."cAgrus: And taking the Spooky Plate from him and defeating the Temple Guardian would stop this?"HViolet: Yes, it would cause the temple to become dormant once more."_Unfortunately, it seems as though someone else will attempt to take the plate before then."?Agrus: We don't have time to waste then. Let's get movin'."MViolet: Push the last statue into place, \PN, and then meet us up ahead."The statue won't budge."Agrus: \PN!"Have you seen Violet?"OShe said she thought someone was followin' us, so we were lookin' for 'em-".But when I turned a corner, she was gone."...",Agrus: Someone appeared in front of ya?"+That must be the person who tailed us!" Did they tell you anythin'?"Agrus: Myron's... dead?"(Violet might be lyin' to us then..."@Though, we can't trust what this random person says either."IThere's a room up ahead, it's the only possible place they could be."@Be careful, and make sure you're prepared before you go in."???: Interesting...">I guess Sloth was right, following them was a great idea~"$It's pointing towards the exit.".Violet: Welcome to the Drowned Catacombs."Agrus: Hold on."6Before we go any further, we have some questions."Violet: Ask away."cAgrus: After we saved you, you mentioned that Rose was in danger because she was a churchgoer."5Violet: Oh yes, Myron will have no mercy on her."3Agrus: Why? What's he have against the Church?"OViolet: Think, ranger. What's the one group that would dislike the Church?"Agrus: ...";Agrus: The Doctrine. Myron's a member of the Doctrine."Violet: So smart."yAlthough, not entirely accurate. Myron isn't a Doctrine member anymore, just that his hatred for the Church remains.";Agrus: There's no telling what he'll do to her then..."Violet: You get the idea."2Although, this may be a blessing in disguise."ñInstead of focusing on completing his plan as fast as possible, he may want to take his time tormenting this Rose and anyone he percieves as her ally."Agrus: Real comfortin'"<Agrus: So, you called this place the Drowned Catacombs?"9Violet: Yes, although it has completely frozen over."AFortunately for us, that'll make it much easier to traverse.",Agrus: Well, let's get on with it then."Violet: After you~")Would you like to reset the statues?".Violet: Welcome to the Drowned Catacombs-"ñInstead of focusing on completing his plan as fast as possible, he may want to take his time tormenting this Rose and anyone he perceives as her ally."Agrus: Real comfortin'."QViolet: Yes, although it betrays its name, as it has completely frozen over."VViolet: Perhaps we'll find out more about each other in these chambers, lost one~"A door opened somewhere!"!Agrus: That's... an Omanyte."/Violet: Glad to see your eyes are working."LAgrus: That's not what I meant, just, why's there a random statue here?"mViolet: Well, there used to be a city on the other side of these catacombs, where Myron's manor resides."bIn order to keep others out, mostly churchfolk, Myron constructed a puzzle in these chambers."®Only a small part of the puzzle remains, and the catacombs' layout has drastically changed over the years, but we'll need to complete what's there in order to progress."'Agrus: I hope it ain't too hard..."¥Violet: Quite simple actually, we just have to move these statues to their corresponding tile somewhere in the catacombs. It's not as obvious as the first tile you see, so be wary."6