kill, nevertheless!":We must take our leave now, but we do have a request."dShago: When I came here, I had a seal on me. It looks like a piece of cloth with writing on it."<I believe Myron stole it and handed it to the Doctrine."<Agrus: So ya want us to keep a look out fer it? Gotcha."<Hyacinth: I will see if we can recover it, don't worry."6We must bid you all farewell now as well, though."%Miss Olga is sure to be worried."Agrus: See y'all around."VHyacinth: I'll let you know once we narrow down the True Spooky Plate's location." We cannot let them have it."3Agrus: I'll see what I can find out too, then."Stay in touch."IHyacinth: Let us know what you find out about the True Spooky Plate."CI'll see if the Church holds any information about it as well." Agrus: Roger that, will do."dKoda: It was nice meeting you all, though I wish it could have been under better circumstances."2Shago: Goodbye. We will meet again I am sure."'Agrus: Finally, this mess is over."mOh, I guess I should've brought it up earlier, but I'm plannin' on headin' back to the mainland with ya."jMy men are staying behind to survey and clean up the area, so we don't have anythin' else to do here.".There's a boat waitin' for us down south.""Let's finally get outta here.".Zossie: Please tell me there's no more..."mPercy: [There seems to be an exit up ahead, it's the only place to go so chances are, Data's there too.]"Zossie: Let's hurry \PN.""Zossie: How can we help them?"7Percy: [For now? Just keep them at bay, but yeah.]"[I want to help them too.]"My throat..."...So thirsty..."Shago: Do good."2Agrus: This should be an easy in an' out job."MI'd be surprised if we found any stragglers but we just gotta make sure."$Koda: Make it a show, will you?"???: Help!"8Agrus: \PN! Take that one! I'll deal with this guy-"Take... to Myron..."$Agrus: Yer alright there, miss?"2???: O-Oh, um, yes I am, thank you very much."wMy name is Violet. I live a little ways up north, but for the past few days, I've been hounded by these... people.">They've even managed to chase me all the way down here..."HAgrus: Yeah, most of 'em are my men, addled by the hail, but these-"-Agrus: Look to be members of the church."6Violet: What would the church be doing down here?"]Agrus: Probably came in search of Rose, a templar who went missin' here a few days back."Violet: ...Oh dear..."-If Myron finds out the church is here..."6Violet: That girl, Rose, is in tremendous danger."0Agrus: Hang on a second, I ain't followin'."*Who's Myron, and why's she in danger?"MViolet: Myron... is my husband. But let's not have this discussion here."Agrus: Hang on, why not?"CViolet: He can hear us out in the Demesne. We must make haste."MAgrus: Meet me in my tent, \PN. Apparently we got a lot to discuss here.".Rose: You are about to battle my brother."fHe is a fierce opponent, but as a last thanks to a temporary comrade, I can give you some advice."ARose: Hyacinth is a Fairy-type specialist, a type most holy."KAzrael, his Galarian Rapidash, is his ace, both fast and hard-hitting."™His signature move is Condescend, a smiting physical blow that deals double the damage if you have any stat reductions. However, it clears the stat reductions afterwards."?It can deal a lot of damage at once, be cognizant of that."DRose: You should be familiar with our surroundings by now, \PN."wThe Bewitched Woods boosts Grass-, Fairy-, and Dark-type moves as well as moves relating to the moon and darkness."íThe field also allows Dark-, Poison-, and Fairy-type moves to hit each other neutrally, and Grass-type moves to hit Steel-types super effectively."jTry not to fall asleep here either, as the nightmares that plague you will sap your health each turn."ÄHyacinth has a hyper offensive strategy, which will be strengthened by the field's nullification of his Fairy-types' weaknesses."íTry to take advantage of his slower support Pokemon before his faster Pokemon come out, or you will find yourself at the other end of his justice."oY