;[	"Tan..."1Do you want the Water-type Pokemon Oshawott?"Yes"NoIu;␀$[[å" Lisa-Marie: We made it \PN!"#Isn't it simply amazing, love?";It's easily many times larger than the Logium Library."zI apologize, I realize we have been together for quite some time, but I simply must explore every inch of this place!"/A newspaper clipping from sixty years ago."w"The skies have suddenly fallen to earth. We have lost all contact with those in the City at the Edge of Forever.""?"Is this yet another disaster caused by the Dasos people?""b"How much longer are we forced to tolerate their existence, a blight upon the true Zakosans?""A captain's log."f"We were doing a routine trip to the island when a rumbling beneath the waves capsized our ship."""I managed to make it to the shore and saw the most incredible thing: A beacon of light shooting straight into the skies.""r"Right in front of me, grass and trees erupted from the earth, the barren land becoming lush within minutes.""The door is locked."5Lisa-Marie: There's so much to explore here \PN!"&Why don't you have a look around?"9???: I apologize for the unfortunate events earlier."AAs recompense, I have opened the door that lies to the west."(Do explore to your heart's content."????: Much work to be done as always, much work to be done."A faded telegram."O"Queen Sola has declared war on the Erimos Region and needs your support!""r"Those who are able to fight, do so, and those who aren't, support the war efforts by donating what you can!"","Soon, the Erimos Region will be ours!""5???: Much work to be done, much work to be done."'???: Do you require my assistance?"..."???: Very well." In honor of our benefactor."A researcher‚Äôs notes."É"I was experimenting close to the- so I could see how the flow of magic affected living things, when I made a fantastic discovery.""b"It looked like a large crystal ball, but when I stepped closer, it was actually a Pok√©mon!""p"It resembled a Voltorb, and gave off occasional sparks, but looked as though it was made of smooth glass.""i"I caught it of course, I‚Äôm sure I can sell it to the library and double my income for this year."" Lisa-Marie: Rather curious."*What could possibly be in this box..."#We must find out \PN, we must!";Perhaps something can provide us with some assistance?"GLisa-Marie: \PN! Was it you who called this lovely Gardevoir here?"???: What is your inquiry?")Lisa-Marie: Right to business I see~"=\PN and I were wondering what was up with this box here."J???: Ah, well, I am afraid that is something I am not able to answer."If that is all-"Lisa-Marie: Wait!"*Are there no details you can tell us?"=???: It holds nothing that could be of value to you two."LWhile I have appreciated your company, it is time for you two to leave."Lisa-Marie: What if..."What if I refuse!")???: ...Then you leave me no choice."8Lisa-Marie: What just happened... Why can't I move?"Who is that?"???: Intruders, Aten."Aten: ...I see."4I suppose it is time for me to fulfill my duty."Formidable."Aten: ..."???: Aten?"???: ..."9I suppose I must be the one to take care of you two-"'???: Hold that thought, Gardevoir."Lisa-Marie: Minerva?"Minerva: At ease."FThese two are no threat, simply two delinquents I happen to know." ???: I see, apologies then." I will get back to my work."Minerva: Now..."&What are you two doing down here?"GThis is something I expect from Lisa-Marie, but not from you, \PN."ZLisa-Marie: Well, I heard rumors of the archives and wanted to see them for myself..."FMinerva: Had you simply asked me, I would have shown them to you."You outrank me after all."-Lisa-Marie: But where's the fun in that?"OIt's so boring in the Forest of Dreams, I wanted to do something exciting!"8Minerva: And how did you manage to anger Gardevoir?"FLisa-Marie: Ah, I just asked them what was in the box back there.""Minerva: ...That would do it."=That box contains the ashes and soul of my father, Aten."Lisa-Marie: Oh."mMinerva: He became the guardian of these archives upon his death, and when I die, I will take his place."xGardevoir was hopelessly devoted to my father, so any attempt to disrupt his remains would definitely draw her ire."*Lisa-Marie: ...My apologies, Minerva."zMinerva: It's no matter, though I would prefer you ask me next time before dragging other people into your endeavors."The archives are free to explore for you two now. Maybe you'll find some information about what we discussed earlier, \PN."Farewell.";Lisa-Marie: What an adventure this was, wasn't it \PN?"BLisa-Marie: Ah, I suppose the cat's out of the bag, isn't it?"&Let me properly introduce myself."QI am Princess Lisa-Marie Alexandra Bastille, the Steel user of the Pantheon."ZI do apologize for taking you for a spin \PN, but I did play my role well, did I not?"BThe helpless damsel falling in love with her brave companion~"eAlas, I am far from helpless, but it is nice to be under another's protection from time to time."OYou will not challenge me for a long time \PN, but I await the day you do."=You will not win, but it should be enjoyable regardless." Farewell, my lovely knight~"=A collection of letters between two unnamed individuals."n"She has grown both dangerously ambitious and beloved by the people. We must keep a close eye on her. -T""Ç"Agreed, but direct opposition will only lead to our vilification. We must remain discrete until our suspicions are confirmed. -L""An old memoir."S"We settled here right after the turn of the century, expecting a quiet life.""O"However, we soon came to realize there is something very, very odd here.""{"Those I spoke to had no recollection of anything past a few years ago as if they had just woken up from a deep slumber..."".???: I believe your companion is waiting."A memoir."x"We erected this library here as a beacon of knowledge and art, far away from the undue influence of the mainland.""É"Our patron saint, Meloetta, will protect this island and the library, and may the knowledge it holds remain for the rest of time."" Your party has been healed!"HEALING PARTY..."An old book."8"Sloth, Pride, Envy, Lust, Wrath, Greed, Gluttony.""G"These are known as the seven deadly sins, the very vices of man.""x"Only when cutting them off from our lives and living as the High Architect wants us to, can we achieve salvation.""A scientific manual."?"Have you ever wanted to create life with your own hands?""["Look no further! This manual will give you detailed instructions on how to play God!""£"We call these human-like golems of our making Anthroparions, and the process to make one is lengthy and involves many sacrifices, but is well worth it in the end-"(The rest of the pages are torn out."An old fairy tale."b"There were once three children, Ena, Dio, and Tria, who lived in a sleepy secluded village.""ä"One day, Ena, the oldest of them, who had grown tired of the days of boredom, asked the other two to follow them to a forbidden orchard.""É"Tria, the youngest of the three, readily agreed in her devotion to Ena, while Dio, straight-laced and serious, refused to follow.""j"Ena and Tria snuck out in the dead of night, arriving at the forbidden orchard just after midnight.""~"Unknown to them, however, the fruit that grew in the orchard was only meant for the gods, and was poisonous to mortals.""v"So upon arriving, Ena climbed a branch and took a bite of the forbidden fruit, falling into an endless slumber.""ã"When the gods came to take Ena with them to the heavens, Tria, wracked with grief, asked the gods to ensure she and Ena would never part.""é"The gods, feeling pity upon Tria, turned her into a great tree that would stretch into the heavens, so she could always feel Ena's presence.""Ç"And in the village, when Dio awoke, her companions had disappeared, but she could see the great tree's branches break the skies.""A tattered diary."("Today was the most wonderful day!""K"My best friends and I visited a small stream and had a picnic there!""2"Apoleia was grumpy as always, but \#H61$&#%-"8???: I'm sorry \PN. This one isn't for you to read."DYou get a splitting headache trying to read this journal entry."???: Why hello, trainer."ZIt has been ages since I have seen anyone other than Minerva Emera grace these halls."f???: My name? I was never given one. Unlike the Pokemon you carry with you, I belong to no human."ΩI have simply been in service of the Emera family since the library was built. I was here before Aten constructed these archives, and will continue to serve them long after Minerva's death."c???: Do not feel pity for me, this was a fate of my choosing, and I have enjoyed the solitude."THowever, if you need me, I shall be more than willing to provide my assistance."0Otherwise, I shall simply continue my work.[å@@@	@
